WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:06.460
Hey youtubers it's Charlie and this week's
Teen Wolf taught us a whole new way to make

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:07.670
a new werewolf.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:10.280
Raise your hand if it made you hungry.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.280
Don't worry I won't judge.

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:12.280
There's actually a whole bunch of stuff to
talk about.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:16.020
There were at least 4 major new plot lines
that started so let's just chomp right in.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:20.540
Hello new people, if you're finding me for
the first time I do weekly Teen Wolf videos.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:21.810
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:26.160
I just made a new playlist in the description
so check there to travel down the youtube

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.120
teen wolf rabbit hole.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:49.520
I'm going 

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:59.620
to start with my top 5 moments and then do
my review.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.320
Careful for spoilers from Episode 3 if you
haven't seen it yet.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:08.600
I'll wait just a sec...Okay, Number 5 - Kate
Took Derek's True Nature

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:10.810
We finally got an answer to his eye color.

00:01:10.810 --> 00:01:13.569
I actually thought it was some conceit of
the de-aging spell.

00:01:13.569 --> 00:01:18.659
But it sounds like Kate did that too him both
to get inside the vault and to take his true

00:01:18.659 --> 00:01:19.659
nature.

00:01:19.659 --> 00:01:23.270
The only reason that comes to mind is that
she needs it to power some other weird ritual.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:28.179
When they said 'True Nature' it made me think
of identity, like Kate took who Derek was,

00:01:28.179 --> 00:01:34.479
so Derek won't be able to do something really
important later this season until he gets

00:01:34.479 --> 00:01:35.479
it back.

00:01:35.479 --> 00:01:36.929
Did you see the way he was acting too.

00:01:36.929 --> 00:01:40.859
I actually thought it was young Derek in old
Derek's body.

00:01:40.859 --> 00:01:44.069
He seemed like he was staring at himself a
lot, like he didn't know himself.

00:01:44.069 --> 00:01:48.359
I have to give props to Tyler Hoechlin for
being able to do a different version of Derek

00:01:48.359 --> 00:01:50.130
without it seeming cheesy.

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:54.259
Let me know what you think we should call
this Derek, like we can call regular Derek,

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:58.079
Derek Prime and this Derek, Shadow Derek.

00:01:58.079 --> 00:02:00.930
It does seem like he's just a fraction of
himself right now.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.759
Like he's in panic mode.

00:02:02.759 --> 00:02:05.739
Number 4 - Lydia Finds The Meat Locker

00:02:05.739 --> 00:02:07.049
If you were confused, don't feel bad.

00:02:07.049 --> 00:02:12.390
It took me till that end reveal of Sean as
a Wendigo.

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:16.450
The mute, played by Joseph Gatt from Game
of Thrones was killing his family because

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:18.140
they were supernatural.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:22.910
It seemed like he did something funky to him
in that bathroom, but really the mute is attacking

00:02:22.910 --> 00:02:24.870
supernatural families in Beacon Hills.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:28.750
It's part of the deadpool kill list and the
benefactor.

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:34.030
The next episode, episode 4 is called "The
Benefactor" so presumably we'll find out who

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:36.920
that is, but when Lydia found all those bodies
in the secret room.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.960
She was finding Sean's families' meat fridge.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.850
Wendigos are from Algonquin mythology.

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:45.160
They were basically cannibal monsters.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:47.870
So that's why those were human bodies.

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:51.110
The family just kept them on ice like you'd
keep steaks on ice.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:54.940
Pretty gross huh, that's why at the end when
he said, "I'm so hungry" he wasn't on drugs

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:55.940
or anything.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.230
He just hadn't fed on human flesh in a long
time.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:01.240
Don't ask what he kept in his gatorade bottle.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:06.750
The other important thing of note here is
Lydia forming a connection with Deputy Parrish.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:11.470
He seemed amazingly sanguine about her supernatural
banshee status even though I don't think he

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:13.110
knows she's a banshee.

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:17.180
She still doesn't understand how her power
works, so they just treat it like a weird

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:18.900
WTF skill she has.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:23.420
I think this is going to turn into more of
a mulder scully relationship where she starts

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:26.210
being more proactive about getting to crime
scenes.

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:29.580
Her power draws her to people who are near
death or who have just died.

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.520
So she's got a super radar for death.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:38.290
I'm really excited to see her get better at
using it.

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:40.810
Number 4 - Malia versus Math

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:45.220
I love the way the show bounces between adorable
and crazy murder so fast.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:48.010
Last week I said Malia was my favorite character
so far this year.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:52.390
I think Lacrosse Kira might give her a run
for her money but the look on her face when

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:54.790
she walked into math class was priceless.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:59.730
I feel like the reaction faces some of the
characters have is what they're really paid

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:00.730
for.

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:04.970
It's a rare art to be able to make faces like
this on command all day.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:09.100
It was like there was a giant middle finger
drawn on the chalk board.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:13.370
It's just a twist on the challenges the characters
face.

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:17.959
Like Malia is more afraid of Math than she
is of Berserkers squishing them like grapes.

00:04:17.959 --> 00:04:22.939
So her ultimate triumph this year will be
slaying Calculus, not the Benefactor.

00:04:22.939 --> 00:04:27.000
But the cool part is that brainiac Stiles
gets to be her wingman.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:32.150
Out on the battlefield he can't do that, he's
like a squishy cloth-wearing mage and she's

00:04:32.150 --> 00:04:34.120
a plate wearing warrior.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:42.800
Except he doesn't have any magic, unless you
consider doing homework magic.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:45.440
Speaking of which Lydia's crazy notes.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:48.139
Those were the same symbols on the computer
screen of the mute.

00:04:48.139 --> 00:04:50.919
Which seem like encoded instructions from
the benefactor.

00:04:50.919 --> 00:04:55.699
I didn't recognize them, but if you think
you know what they are just write it in the

00:04:55.699 --> 00:04:56.699
comments.

00:04:56.699 --> 00:04:59.330
Number 3 - The Mute Is Killing Peoples

00:04:59.330 --> 00:05:00.770
So here's a weird thought.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:05.610
If he has no mouth, how did he speak to Sean
at the beginning of the episode when he trapped

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:06.659
him in the bathroom?

00:05:06.659 --> 00:05:09.650
Or was that voice coming from the benefactor
and not the mute?

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:15.300
We'll probably have to wait to find out as
we haven't seen the mute communicate with

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:19.550
anyone directly, beyond making the whisper
motion to Scott.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:23.490
He's pretty clearly getting instructions from
the benefactor via that weird computer pipeline

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:24.490
he plugged into.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.629
It's like some kind of magical cyber gear.

00:05:26.629 --> 00:05:31.139
Like a combination of technology and magic.

00:05:31.139 --> 00:05:38.189
There was actually a Marvel "What If" storyline
where Tony Stark became Doctor Strange and

00:05:38.189 --> 00:05:42.980
inscribed all these magical runes on his Iron
Man suit so that he could automate spells.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:48.819
I don't think we'll see anything like that
on Teen Wolf, but I really want to find out

00:05:48.819 --> 00:05:51.750
how the benefactor is using the internet to
program the mute.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.030
He seems like he has cognition and free will.

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:57.509
But he also kind of seems like a flesh and
blood robot being controlled with a magical

00:05:57.509 --> 00:05:58.599
remote.

00:05:58.599 --> 00:06:01.400
Number 2 - Kira Joins the Lacrosse Team

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.939
Even though lacrosse felt like the challenge
for her this week and the relationship with

00:06:04.939 --> 00:06:06.120
Scott was the reward.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:07.910
It felt like it should have been the other
way around.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:12.470
Like she had to overcome Scott's derpy-ness
and as a reward she'd get to join the lacrosse

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:13.470
team.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.189
Scott's the real challenge for her.

00:06:15.189 --> 00:06:16.939
Lacrosse is too easy for her to be a challenge.

00:06:16.939 --> 00:06:20.759
Just look at her twirl her lacrosse stick,
I could watch a gif of this for hours.

00:06:20.759 --> 00:06:24.300
I can't wait to see her decapitate someone
with it.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.470
The whole parent's moving plot seems like
a dead end.

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:29.150
Like they might just drop that, because she's
not going to leave the series and she's not

00:06:29.150 --> 00:06:33.242
going to move in with Lydia or Malia but I
don't mind.

00:06:33.242 --> 00:06:39.400
I am so much more excited about Lacrosse now
that it's not going to be a straight up redo

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.180
of Freshman year lacrosse.

00:06:41.180 --> 00:06:45.420
With Kira on the team now I feel like the
Lacrosse scenes will be all about her, which

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.849
is way more fun than watching Scott go alpha
over everyone.

00:06:48.849 --> 00:06:53.259
That's what season 1 was all about, him using
werewolf powers on the field.

00:06:53.259 --> 00:06:54.259
So I'm glad Kira is going to make it interesting.

00:06:54.259 --> 00:06:57.939
and my Number 1 WTF moment, of course - Scott
Bites Liam

00:06:57.939 --> 00:07:00.809
Full disclosure, I knew this was going to
happen a long time ago.

00:07:00.809 --> 00:07:06.150
The creator of the show, Jeff Davis was talking
about Liam becoming Scott's new beta all summer.

00:07:06.150 --> 00:07:08.310
I just didn't know how it was going to happen.

00:07:08.310 --> 00:07:09.680
How he was going to give him the bite.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:16.460
I thought it was a really cool twist, Scott
would have never willingly bitten someone.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:21.080
The real fun part was Scott's reaction after
the mute left.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:25.090
There were two big moments in the episode
where Scott's Brain just went offline and

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:28.499
then had like a violent reboot.

00:07:28.499 --> 00:07:31.930
The first time was when he unconsciously kissed
Kira on the way to class and then was like

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:33.069
wait what?!

00:07:33.069 --> 00:07:38.430
And then the second time was the Bite, where
he was like WTF Derp?!

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:41.869
I'd call him Derp Scott in this episode, but
he was being a hero and I love the idea of

00:07:41.869 --> 00:07:44.249
Scott having a Beta that's a brand new character.

00:07:44.249 --> 00:07:49.619
So I forgive him for being a space cadet.

00:07:49.619 --> 00:07:50.659
Here's my big question for you?

00:07:50.659 --> 00:07:54.550
Looking back at all your favorite Scott moments
in the last couple of seasons, how many times

00:07:54.550 --> 00:08:00.449
do you think he's been mentally out to lunch
and then did that delayed reaction face?

00:08:00.449 --> 00:08:03.949
And do you think this is like a really big
issue with him not being able to think in

00:08:03.949 --> 00:08:04.960
the moment?

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:13.210
or do you think it's just him acting on instinct
and he's not just totally spacing out during

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:15.419
important moments.

00:08:15.419 --> 00:08:19.999
Overall I gave the episode a B plus, This
was my favorite episode of the season so far.

00:08:19.999 --> 00:08:23.350
I love the Liam character so far but I feel
like we won't really get to know him until

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:25.129
he's part of the pack.

00:08:25.129 --> 00:08:37.030
Lacrosse Kira wins so hard with me and Malia
and her Markers were a nice misdirect for

00:08:37.030 --> 00:08:41.352
what's probably going to turn into a serious
problem later when she figures out Peter is

00:08:41.352 --> 00:08:42.352
her father.

00:08:42.352 --> 00:08:43.352
Remember Stiles looking at the people chart
on her wall.

00:08:43.352 --> 00:08:45.830
It's too bad this airs during the summer,
because I'd love to see a Halloween episode

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:48.180
where they all dress up as Avengers.

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:52.500
You guys can pick who gets to be who, but
Scott has to be Captain America and Lydia

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:54.430
has to be Scarlet Witch.

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:55.680
Everybody else is up for grabs.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:00.700
Maybe Malia could be She-Hulk or Angela.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:04.140
I feel like there's this weird pattern emerging
with the characters, like they face challenges

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:09.690
and if they defeat them.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:14.010
Like if Malia defeats Math, she gets to be
a real person.

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:19.030
She's like Pinnochio trying to become a normal
human and Kira is trying to fit in, so if

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:24.950
she can kick ass at lacrosse and defeat Scott's
reluctance she'll get a relationship and everyone's

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:25.950
acceptance.

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:31.990
Let me know what you think Lydia's and Stiles
rewards are if they can defeat their challenges.

00:09:31.990 --> 00:09:35.650
So this week was kind of crazy with Guardians
of the Galaxy stuff going on, but I'm going

00:09:35.650 --> 00:09:43.310
to try to do an extra Teen Wolf bonus video
next Monday.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.600
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:51.600
I've also got a playlist in the description.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:55.670
Right now click here for my Episode 2 video
and click here for my episode 1 video.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:09:56.670
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:56.870
High Fives!

